fields.prculley\n\n 2016-06-01 14:12\n\nmanager:
I didn't mean to start a firestorm; I do regard this a 'trivial' issue. However some other gramps scripts have the shebang set for python3. For example various test scripts and the make.py in addons-source has
#! /usr/bin/env python3

My understanding is that for those shells that understand shebang, the appropriate version gets called. For others, well user has to deal.

